{%- comment -%}
  An affiliation logo set inline with running text.

  Lives in an include rather than inline in the Markdown so the `relative_url`
  filter stays out of `_pages/*.md`: the link checker reads those files as raw
  text, before Liquid runs, and would treat `{{ ... }}` as a literal filename.

  The markup is captured and emitted through `strip_newlines` so it always
  reaches the page as a single line. Kramdown treats a raw tag broken across
  lines inside a paragraph as plain text and escapes it, so a reformat of this
  file (Prettier wraps long tags) would otherwise silently break the page.

  Params: file (required, name under /assets/img/), modifier, alt.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- capture logo_markup -%}
<img
  class="inline-logo{% if include.modifier %} inline-logo--{{ include.modifier }}{% endif %}"
  src="{{ include.file | prepend: '/assets/img/' | relative_url }}"
  alt="{{ include.alt }}"
  {%- unless include.alt %} aria-hidden="true"{% endunless %}
>
{%- endcapture -%}
{{- logo_markup | strip_newlines -}}
